.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-remove - Remove a team member


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team remove <team> <account> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a team member

.PP
Remove one member from a team at the expected generation. Team resource access supplied through membership is withdrawn for that account.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant machine use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
